description: Where this onboarding stands, and what the current stage asks for. Start every session here.
---

Run:

```bash
asgard-cli next
```

Read the whole output, including the open questions and open work it prints
underneath - those are what the repository says is unfinished, and they are not
derived from the same signals as the stage.

**The stage is an opinion, not an instruction.** It comes from a fixed set of
file-level signals. You can read more: `AGENTS.md`, the living spec under
`docs/spec/`, `docs/open-questions.md`, what the charts actually declare, and
what the customer said an hour ago. **Where you disagree with it, you are
usually right** - an onboarding is not linear.

If the projects are not all in the same stage, `next` says so and names each
one. The stage it leads with is the earliest gap anywhere, which is the right
thing to do next and is **not** a statement about the repository as a whole.

To reach guidance by subject instead of by position:

```bash
asgard-cli find "<what you are actually deciding>"
```
